  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "$3\\sqrt[3]{q}-4\\sqrt{q}+2\\sqrt[3]{q}+2\\sqrt{q}=$",
  "worked_solution": "We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{q}$ terms together, and the two $\\sqrt{q}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt[3]{q}-4\\sqrt{q}+2\\sqrt[3]{q}+2\\sqrt{q} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt[3]{q}+2\\sqrt[3]{q}-4\\sqrt{q}+2\\sqrt{q} & = \\\\ (3+2)\\sqrt[3]{q}+(-4+2)\\sqrt{q} & = \\\\ 5\\sqrt[3]{q}-2\\sqrt{q} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we cannot combine the $\\sqrt[3]{q}$ and $\\sqrt{q}$ terms.",
